# Collisions: 80 N down on the flange in the middle of a fast move (J1 at
# ~50 deg/s, J6 ~150 deg/s) is detected on J3 within ~10 ms and LinuxCNC
# goes to estop (off_reason 2); with the drives disabled the detector
# resets. At rest (re-enabled where the arm
# stopped) the stiction band makes it less sensitive: 120 N down is still
# found within ~10 ms (on the wrist at this pose), 10 N is not (sensitivity
# sweep in host/arm/README.md). Simulation: ideal sensors.
@program arm/arm_sim
@args arm/arcmate/arcmate.arm
detector arm/arcmate/model_perturbed.arm
lcnc 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1
run 1.5
move 2 60 30 30 90 -40 180
run 0.8
mark
print time
force 6 0 0 -80 0 0 0.1
run 0.3
print coll off
force off
lcnc 0
run 0.5
print coll
lcnc 1
run 2.0
mark
print time
force 6 0 0 -10 0 0 0.1
run 0.5
print coll off
force 6 0 0 -120 0 0 0.1
run 0.3
print time coll off fault
@expect arm.time[1] ~ 2.8 0.0005
@expect arm.off_reason[1] == 2
@expect arm.off_joint[1] == 3
@expect arm.en[1] == 0
@expect arm.coll_time[1] > 2.8
@expect arm.coll_time[1] < 2.82
@expect arm.coll[2] == 0
@expect arm.coll[3] == 0
@expect arm.off_reason[2] == 0
@expect arm.off_reason[3] == 2
@expect arm.off_joint[3] >= 4
@expect arm.time[2] ~ 5.6 0.0005
@expect arm.coll_time[4] > 6.1
@expect arm.coll_time[4] < 6.13
@expect max arm.fault5 == 0
@reject ^ERROR
